Turkey in 60 Seconds · History in 60 Seconds series · Silkscreen Travel Poster style

Picture: drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Print engine engine/silk.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (MIT).
Landmarks (a ring of T-shaped stone pillars, a walled capital on a ridge with a chariot, a harbour city with a great column and
galleys, a domed church on a ring of windows, triple land walls under smoke with a cannon, a domed mosque with four minarets and
tulips, a castle hill and an assembly hall on a new boulevard, a strait with a suspension bridge, ferries and balloons) are original
stylised silhouettes drawn as simple paths, not traced from photographs. No logos, no flags or emblems, no maps or borders.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/):
  Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / Google Fonts
  Outfit — Rodrigo Fuenzalida / Google Fonts

Voice: Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george. Checked with faster-whisper (MIT), model base.en.

Music (original score, music/compose.py): oboe (in the role of the zurna), harp (in the role of the kanun), bassoon, bass drum
(davul) and frame drum played from recorded samples through core/audio/sampler.py (Lemo-Opuscar, MIT).
  Samples (CC0): VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios), Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios).
Sound (mix.py): paper swish, stamps, tiles clicking over, wind, birds, hooves, harbour water, gulls, a city murmur, distant booms,
a ferry horn, traffic: synthesised in code.
Mastering: FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL) via imageio-ffmpeg.

